<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 1.513 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 1.513 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 1.513 billion pesos from the secondary market on Thursday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and three repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    364 days   20.50 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    182 days</p>
<p>    150 million     91 days</p>
<p>The repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    450 million     35 days</p>
<p>    450 million     21 days</p>
<p>    163 million	1 day</p>
<p>	  *Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
